  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "In the 5-digit number $a6a41$ each of the $a$'s represents the same digit. If the number is divisible by 9, then the digit represented by $a$ is",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$3$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$7$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$6$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$8$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$5$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Digit sum",
    "body": "The digit sum $2a+11$ must be a multiple of $9$. With $0\\le a\\le9$, $2a+11$ lies between $11$ and $29$, and the only multiple of $9$ with the right parity (odd) is $27$. So $2a=16$, $a=8$. Check: $86841=9\\times9649$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 8**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
   "number-theory"
