  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "In the figure $AB=AF$ and $BC=CD$. The size of angle $DBF$ is",
  "image": "qimages/samf/senior-2003-r1/q16.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$30^\\circ$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$45^\\circ$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$22.5^\\circ$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$60^\\circ$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$67.5^\\circ$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Angle chase",
    "body": "Let $\\angle ABF=\\angle AFB=x$ and $\\angle CBD=\\angle CDB=y$. Then $\\angle A=180^\\circ-2x$ and $\\angle C=180^\\circ-2y$. Triangle $ACE$ has a right angle at $E$, so $\\angle A+\\angle C=90^\\circ$: $360^\\circ-2x-2y=90^\\circ$, giving $x+y=135^\\circ$. Hence $\\angle DBF=180^\\circ-x-y=45^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $45^\\circ$**"
   }
  ],
