  },
  "grade": "10-12",
  "points": 5,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "In the figure, rectangle $ABCD$ has dimensions as shown ($AB=2$, $AD=1$). The area of rectangle $BDFE$ is",
  "image": "qimages/samf/senior-2003-r1/q17.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$\\sqrt2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$\\sqrt5$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$\\frac{4}{\\sqrt5}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$1+\\sqrt2$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Distance from C to BD",
    "body": "The side $FE$ of rectangle $BDFE$ is parallel to $BD$ and passes through $C$, so the width $BE$ equals the distance from $C$ to the line $BD$. Triangle $BCD$ has area $\\frac12\\cdot1\\cdot2=1$ and base $BD=\\sqrt5$, so its height from $C$ is $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt5}$. Hence the area is $BD\\cdot BE=\\sqrt5\\cdot\\frac2{\\sqrt5}=2$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 2**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Similar triangles",
    "body": "Triangles $BCD$ and $BEC$ are similar right triangles, so $\\frac{BE}{BC}=\\frac{CD}{BD}$, i.e. $BE=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt5}$. Area $=\\sqrt5\\cdot\\frac2{\\sqrt5}=2$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 2**"
   }
  ],
