  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "If the digits $k,m,n$ of the 3-digit number $kmn$ satisfy $64k+8m+n=403$, then the number $kmn$ is",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$623$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$563$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$403$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$643$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "not possible to be uniquely determined"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Divisibility by 8",
    "body": "$n=403-64k-8m\\equiv403\\equiv3\\pmod8$, and $n$ is a digit, so $n=3$. Then $8k+m=50$; so $m\\equiv50\\equiv2\\pmod 8$, giving $m=2$ ($m=10$ is not a digit), and $k=6$. The number is $623$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 623**"
   }
  ],
